qumracapital-jfrog:greenhouse:7625966.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps and shaping how software is delivered, helping the world’s leading companies innovate faster and safer. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software”.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Director of Engineering to lead JFrog’s agentic capabilities across the platform, including the JFrog AI Assistant, MCP Server, and a rapidly expanding ecosystem of autonomous workflows. This is a high-impact role shaping how developers and organizations build, secure, and deliver software—through enterprise-grade AI that can take action, operate safely, and scale across SaaS and self-hosted environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Director of Engineering at JFrog, you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the engineering group delivering AI capabilities across the JFrog platform, powering customer-facing agentic experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the vision and drive the execution for JFrog AI Assistant, MCP Server, and platform-wide agent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship enterprise-grade AI—secure, reliable, and observable—running in SaaS and self-hosted environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the quality bar for AI delivery, including evaluation, safety guardrails, and continuous improvement loops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of LLMs, AI agents, and DevOps automation trends, translating innovation into platform differentiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and mentor high-performing teams and a culture of execution, automation, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Security, and engineering leaders to drive adoption and make measurable customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Director of Engineering at JFrog, you need...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in software engineering, with at least 5 years in leadership roles managing diverse R&amp;amp;D teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Software Development: strong experience in building and managing scalable systems using languages such as Go, Python, Java, or Node.js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering scalable cloud / SaaS services, operating in multi-cloud (AWS, Azure, GCP) and hybrid-cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading AI product (assistants, copilots, LLM-integrated workflows)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership, communication, stakeholder, and customer management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for empowering developers and enabling productivity through platform engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps / DevSecOps experience — strong advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset, with continuous learning in AI and agentic technologies&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

remotely-bridgebio:greenhouse:5144756007.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Mavericks Wanted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;When was the last time you achieved the impossible? If that thought feels overwhelming, you might want to pause here, but if it sparks excitement...read on&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;In 2015, we pioneered a “moneyball for biotech” approach, pooling projects and promising early-stage research from academia together under one financial umbrella to reduce risk and unleash innovation. This model allows science and small teams of experts to lead the way. We build bridges to groundbreaking advancements in rare&amp;nbsp;disease, and&amp;nbsp;develop life-changing medicines for patients with unmet needs as fast as humanly possible. &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Together we define white space, push boundaries, and empower people to solve problems. If you&#39;re someone who defies convention, join us and work alongside some of the most respected minds in the industry. Together, we&#39;ll&amp;nbsp;ask&amp;nbsp;&quot;why not?&quot; and help reengineer the future of biopharma. At BridgeBio, we value curiosity and experimentation—including the ethical &amp;amp; thoughtful use of AI to improve clarity, speed, and quality of work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;u&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BridgeBio is seeking a highly motivated and experienced individual to join as an Associate Director or Director of Strategic Finance. The role reports to Strategic Finance and Investor Relations and will be instrumental in driving the company’s corporate finance and capital markets efforts to support growth and enhance shareholder value. The position is designed for an individual who can operate at the intersection of science, strategy, and finance, and translate complex analyses into clear recommendations for executive leadership and the Board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is focused on evaluating and executing strategic and financial opportunities at BridgeBio. A successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional problem-solving ability, strong independent judgment, and the capacity to translate complex scientific and financial analyses into clear, decisive recommendations for executive leadership. We are looking for a hardworking and collaborative candidate that can thrive in a fast-paced environment with strong attention to detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;u&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transaction Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead end-to-end evaluation and execution of strategic transactions, including licensing, M&amp;amp;A, structured financings, and asset-level partnerships—from opportunity framing through diligence, valuation, and negotiation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capital Allocation &amp;amp; Strategic Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with senior leadership to evaluate key business and financial decisions through insights, scenario modeling, and assessment of strategic options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decision Modeling &amp;amp; Valuation: &lt;/strong&gt;Apply advanced valuation frameworks (e.g., real options, probabilistic modeling) to inform investment decisions and transaction structuring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Investor Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Synthesize complex analyses into clear recommendations for senior leadership, the Board, and external stakeholders, including materials supporting capital markets activity and strategic transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investor Relations &amp;amp; Consensus Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Support investor relations activities through analysis of Street models, management of external expectations, development of investor materials, and preparation for earnings and key corporate events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;u&gt;Where You&#39;ll Work&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an in-person role and requires in-office collaboration 4-5 days per week, primarily in our Palo Alto office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who You Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mission-oriented: Motivated by the opportunity to help advance life-saving medicines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and hardworking: Thoughtful, diligent, committed to delivering high-quality work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focused on results: Willing to take ownership and see projects through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multitasker: Comfortable working across several high stakes workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated. Thrives in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-oriented. Values collaboration and supports others across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in science, engineering, business, finance, economics, or a related analytical discipline required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced scientific or clinical degree, including PhD, MD, PharmD, or equivalent experience, strongly preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years of experience in management consulting with demonstrated progression to team leadership roles (e.g., Engagement Manager or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience conducting commercial diligence on biotechnology assets&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional problem-solving skills with a first-principles approach to complex scientific and business questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical expertise translating clinical and commercial insights into diligence-grade analyses and transaction materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous problems and drive them to clear, actionable conclusions in high-stakes settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in financial modeling and valuation is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with advanced techniques such as real options analysis, Monte Carlo simulation, or other quantitative frameworks is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and persuasive communicator, both in writing and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with industry data platforms like IQVIA and/or financial data platforms like Bloomberg or Capital IQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At BridgeBio, we strive to provide a market-competitive total rewards package, including base pay, an annual performance bonus, company equity, and generous health benefits. Below is the anticipated salary range for candidates for this role who will work in California. The final salary offered to a successful candidate will depend on several factors that may include but are not limited to the type and length of experience within the job, type, and length of experience within the industry, educational background, location of residence and performance during the interview process. BridgeBio is a multi-state employer, and this salary range may not reflect positions based in other states.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$222,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$274,800 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a global company, our comprehensive benefits may vary based on location.&amp;nbsp; &lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We have high expectations for our team members. We make sure those working hard for patients are rewarded and cared for in return.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
